    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/render-structured-data.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/render-structured-data.mjs [--retry-failed] [--storefinder-only] [--build-only]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Skipped: FSA ratings pages, OSM, Wikidata, Wikipedia (CC BY-SA), Companies House, Land Registry, register pages, social networks, the live canarywharf.com (Imperva challenge).",
    "robots.txt per RFC 9309 (token glitchcan-cwplans, else *); an unreachable robots.txt means no visit; the failure is classed by its cause (dns, tls, timeout, 5xx).",
    "Order: store pages, then pages the plain crawl got no structured data from, then the rest; Internet Archive CWG copies read from cache with scripts off.",
    "A cookie banner is clicked only when the page shows no structured data and a known consent button is visible. No logins, no forms other than a store-finder search box with a UK postcode.",
    "Store finder: a result link is followed only when its text, URL or card names the branch postcode, a street or mall phrase of the branch, or (for a brand with one branch here) Canary Wharf.",
    "Blocks over 200 kB are dropped and counted.",
    "User-Agent: a desktop Chrome string plus \" glitchcan-cwplans/0.1 (+https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam)\"; robots.txt fetched with Node (15 s timeout), else through Chromium.",
    "Each page: wait for load and network idle, at most 20 s (CAP_MS), then 1.5 s (LATE_MS) for late JSON-LD.",
    "Store finders: one postcode search per brand and postcode; the postcode is the branch's own, else E14 4QT (owner rule 2026-10-03: \"we are permitted per industry convention to submit storefinder forms with UK postcodes\"). No other forms.",
    "Resumable: a URL with a stored result in data/raw/rendered/ is not rendered again unless --retry-failed and its failure was transient."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/crawl-sites"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "structured",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The skip list and the consent-button list are written in the tool; store-finder searches follow the owner rule of 2026-10-03."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/extract-structured-data",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "extract-structured-data",
   "dct:description": "Cleans each JSON-LD block (jsonld-clean.mjs: wrappers, comments, trailing and missing commas, control characters, invalid escapes, concatenated values, HTML entities, remote schema.org contexts inlined as {\"@vocab\": \"https://schema.org/\"}, @graph unwrapped, http://schema.org/ normalised; every repair counted by class), converts it with Factoidal jsonldToRdf, converts microdata JSON to RDF (schema.org vocabulary), parses RDFa N-Triples with Factoidal, loads one named graph per page, writes all.nq, then runs SPARQL with Factoidal for types, names, telephones, opening hours and their specifications, addresses, geo and events, and attributes each node to the registry entities that link to the page.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/../../third_party/cwplans-structured-data/pages"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/../../third_party/cwplans-structured-data/index.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/buildings.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/brands/branches.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/brands/storelocator.json"
    },
    {
