   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs walk [--details] [--refresh]; NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs refs; NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs probe [id ...] (needs npm install --no-save xlsx@0.18.5); node magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs triage; NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/walk-london-datastore.mjs harvest [key ...] [--refresh]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Catalogue: publisher = organisation (logo title), else CKAN maintainer, else custom.author; geo = custom.geo (spatial granularity); update_frequency = custom.update_frequency; resource format = file extension; resource URL = https://data.london.gov.uk/download/{dataset}/{id}/{file}. Not kept: descriptions, contact names and emails, logos.",
    "Licence class: OGL v2/v3 -> ogl; Creative Commons Attribution -> cc-by; ODC Attribution -> odc-by; Public Domain, PDDL -> public-domain (these four are open); CC BY-SA and ODbL -> share-alike (never harvested, CLAUDE.md); CC Non-Commercial and All Rights Reserved -> restricted; TfL Transport Data Service Licence -> other; empty -> none (never harvested).",
    "Relevance, first match: zone-place (title or tag names a place in the 3D model box; \"upon Thames\", \"Thames Estuary\", \"Thames Gateway\", \"Thamesmead\" removed first); zone-borough (names only Tower Hamlets, Southwark, Lewisham, Greenwich, Newham, City of London); other-area (names 1-3 places, none in the zone); london-fine (geo finer than a borough, or with no geo a ward/LSOA/MSOA/OA/postcode/UPRN/TOID word or a spatial format); london-borough; london-coarse; unknown.",
    "Have: a dataset id or slug in a committed file of magpie/cwplans: data-register.json, pipeline.json, tools, data files -> held; a .md note, feeds catalogues, the 2026-10-03 survey -> listed; an \"excluded\" list or a survey \"left out\" line -> excluded-before; else new. feeds/london-datastore/ and the generated docs are not read.",
    "Sensitive (catalogued, score 0, never harvested): title names homicide, victims, strip or intimate searches, suicide, custody, stop and search, hate crime, domestic abuse, sexual offences, safeguarding, missing persons, rough sleeping (CHAIN), bariatric incidents.",
    "Score = relevance weight (zone-place 5, zone-borough 4, london-fine 3, london-borough 1.5, unknown 1, london-coarse 0.3, other-area 0) x max(theme value, 0.5) x recency (newest resource year >= 2024: 1, >= 2021: 0.8, >= 2016: 0.5, else 0.3) x (machine-readable format ? 1 : 0.4) x (a join key finer than a borough ? 1.3 : 1) x (open ? 1 : 0) x (held 0, listed 0.8, new 1).",
    "Harvest zone: a feature is kept when its geometry meets the 3D model box (BNG E 532400-539900, N 176700-182300): a vertex inside, an edge crossing (Liang-Barsky) or the box centre inside a polygon. Whole geometries kept, not cut; whole_in_zone and in_cw (meets the Canary Wharf registry box -0.03, 51.498, -0.005, 51.51) are added.",
    "Coordinates: GeoPackage SRS 27700, or a custom definition on Airy 1830 with the BNG projection (srs_id 100000) -> BNG; output WGS84 to 6 decimal places through OSTN15. CSV points: a row is WGS84 when |x| <= 180 and |y| <= 90, else BNG; empty or zero coordinates -> no_geometry.",
    "Dropped fields: names matching e-mail, phone, contact, fax, mobile, owner name, person (none matched in the 13 harvested files). uprn_suspect: a UPRN field with an exponent or 9+ digits ending in 5+ zeros (F22). The Brownfield Register is read from its CSV, not the GPKG (F23).",
    "Network: one request at a time over the whole tool, at least 1.1 s apart; up to 6 tries with Retry-After or a doubling pause on 429, 5xx and network errors; User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1. robots.txt disallows only /debug, /manage/, /login, /logout.",
    "Details walk (--details, 2026-10-04, all 1,305 datasets): /api/v3/dataset/<id> adds per resource the publisher's generic format (kind) and an md5 hash, and per dataset the description; the catalogue keeps a details member (resource count, kinds, archivedAt, nextReviewDate, geo, the granularity words and zone place names found in the description, resources only in the details record). The description text itself is not kept. Result: 0 archived, 0 resources missing from the export, geo identical to the export for all 1,305.",
    "Zone references (refs): a code is a zone code when a live or terminated ONSPD (August 2026) postcode whose grid reference lies in the 3D model box carries it, or when its polygon in the Datastore's Statistical GIS Boundary Files (20od9: LSOA/MSOA 2021, OA/LSOA/MSOA/wards 2011, wards 2014 and 2018) meets the box. Zone UPRNs: OS Open UPRN X/Y in the box; zone TOIDs: the LIDS TopographicArea TOIDs of those UPRNs (raw cache only)."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [
    "F22",
    "F23"
   ],
   "cwp:judgement": "The harvest shortlist (the HARVEST table in the tool) was chosen by hand from the ranked triage: open, relevant, new, machine-readable, not geometry-only where an alternative exists; the choices and the ranked backlog with reasons are in feeds/london-datastore/README.md."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/amend-uprns",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "amend-uprns",
   "dct:description": "Copies a spreadsheet-sourced file and amends only the UPRN cells that a spreadsheet rounded (F22). Every cell is classified (rounded: scientific notation, or 9+ digits ending in 5+ zeros; catalogued only: empty, text, decimal, out of range, padded, duplicate across venues, not in OS Open UPRN, over 150 m from its OS Open UPRN point, and per-layer constant position offsets, F25). Each rounded venue is recovered by the first route that gives exactly one candidate inside the range the rounded value allows: (a) the same dataset in other formats, layers and releases, (b) OS Open UPRN points in the venue's OSM building outline, (c) registers with UPRNs; else (d) unknown with the reason. Writes the amended copy beside the source and an amendments file with one entry per changed cell, every unknown, the catalogue, the rules and the measured precision of routes a and b (each valid 12-digit UPRN rounded to 3 and 6 digits and recovered blind).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/feeds/london-datastore/cultural-infrastructure/cultural-infrastructure.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/feeds/london-datastore/catalogue.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/lds-23697",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/23697/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "GET every CSV, zip and venue GeoPackage of the dataset (all revisions; CEZ files skipped)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/lds-2ko88",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/2ko88/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "GET every CSV, zip and venue GeoPackage (the 2018-2020 releases)"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/lds-2zj1y",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://data.london.gov.uk/download/2zj1y/<resource id>/<file>",
     "dct:description": "GET the 2024 LGBTQ+ venues CSV"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/gla-cim-arcgis",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://gis.london.gov.uk/arcgis/rest/services/apps/Cultural_infrastructure_2023_for_webapp_verified/MapServer/<layer>/query",
     "dct:description": "GET each of 37 layers, zone envelope in EPSG:27700, outFields=*, outSR=4326, f=geojson, pages of 1,000"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/registry/osopenuprn_202609_csv.zip"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/docklands/osm-clip.json.gz"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/buildings.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/registers/gias.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/registers/ods.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/registers/active-places.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/uk_os_OSTN15_NTv2_OSGBtoETRS.tif"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/feeds/london-datastore/cultural-infrastructure/cultural-infrastructure.uprn-amended.geojson"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/feeds/london-datastore/cultural-infrastructure/cultural-infrastructure.uprn-amendments.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/uprn-amend/"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/amend-uprns.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/amend-uprns.mjs cultural-infrastructure [--refresh]; generic: node magpie/cwplans/tools/amend-uprns.mjs --in <file> --uprn-field <f> --id-field <f[,f]> [--ref a:<file>]... [--ref c:<file>]... [--open-uprn <zip|csv>] [--footprints <osm-clip.json.gz>] --out <copy> --amendments <json>",
   "cwp:kind": "transform",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "The source file is read, never written; a value that is not in a rounded class is never changed.",
    "Range: Excel rounds to k significant digits; the true value lies within half a unit of the last kept digit (1.00023E+11 -> [100022500000, 100023500000); plain 200000000000 -> k = non-zero prefix -> [150000000000, 250000000000)); rounded forms of the same venue in other releases narrow it by intersection.",
    "Venue: rows with the same normalised name within 50 m are one venue; candidates are pooled and every row gets the same answer.",
    "Route a: same normalised name (or one contains the other, 8+ characters) and point within 50 m (or the same address1 without a point); exactly one distinct full UPRN in range.",
    "Route b: the smallest OSM building outline containing the venue point (none: OS Open UPRN points within 10 m); in a layer with a measured constant offset the moved point is tried too; exactly one OS Open UPRN point in range.",
    "Route c: as route a over GIAS, ODS and Active Places rows with UPRNs.",
    "Confidence: high = route a, exact name, OS Open UPRN point of the candidate within 150 m of the venue (or of the venue moved by its layer offset); medium = other route a, route c, route b with the candidate within 1 m of the venue's own point in an outline of at most 25 UPRN points; low = other route b. High and medium applied; low recorded, not applied.",
    "Two or more candidates: never chosen between; the venue stays unknown with the candidates listed."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/walk-london-datastore"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "feeds",
   "cwp:fault": [
    "F22",
    "F25"
   ],
   "cwp:judgement": "The thresholds (50 m, 150 m, 10 m, 1 m, 25 UPRN points) and the confidence levels are hand choices, recorded in the tool header constants and in skills/cwplans-london-datastore/SKILL.md \"Amending rounded UPRNs\"; the measured precision that supports them is in the amendments file meta.validation. The 2025 Cultural Infrastructure Map (2rj5o, no licence on the Datastore) was left out by decision."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/check-fp16-shaders",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "check-fp16-shaders",
   "dct:description": "Checks the 3D page's shaders for what a phone GPU would do differently from the headless SwiftShader renderer: opens the page in headless Chromium, captures every compiled shader source, and counts each program's uniform rows, varyings, samplers and attributes against the WebGL 1 minimums; then re-runs the shaders' risky maths (hashes, time arguments, far positions, derivatives) in Node with every intermediate rounded to IEEE binary16, beside fp32.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/docklands/index.html"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/docklands/sky.js"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/check-fp16-shaders.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node magpie/cwplans/tools/check-fp16-shaders.mjs [--no-browser]",
   "cwp:kind": "check",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "fp16: round to nearest, ties to even, 10-bit mantissa, exponents -14 to 15 with subnormals, overflow to infinity (Node 22 has no Math.f16round).",
    "A case fails only for a shader declared mediump (on a phone mediump may be fp16); cases for shaders that ask for highp where present (HIP, PRE) are reported as notes, because every OpenGL ES 3 GPU has highp in fragment shaders.",
    "Each case quotes the shader text it mirrors; when that text is gone from the page the case is reported STALE and the tool fails.",
    "Uniform rows are counted without packing (every float, vec2 and vec3 a whole row), so a real count is at most the one shown; minimums: 128 vertex and 16 fragment uniform vectors, 8 varyings, 8 texture units, 8 attributes.",
    "Writes nothing; exit 1 on a failing or stale case."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "imagery",
   "cwp:fault": []
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/fetch-crown-lighting",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "fetch-crown-lighting",
   "dct:description": "Finds the press pages and dated open photos that can say which colour a Canary Wharf crown (One Canada Square's halo first) showed on a given night: CWG sitemaps filtered by slug, archived copies of those pages, and Wikimedia Commons night photos with capture date and licence. The colour itself is judged by hand (activity crown-lighting-judgement).",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/cwg-press",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://cwg.com/press-release-sitemap.xml, https://cwg.com/community_news-sitemap.xml (direct); https://web.archive.org/web/2026id_/https://canarywharf.com/news-sitemap.xml",
     "dct:description": "Yoast sitemaps; every <loc> outside /wp-content/"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/cwg-press",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://archive.org/wayback/available?url=… then https://web.archive.org/web/{timestamp}id_/{url}",
     "dct:description": "the closest archived copy of each candidate page, under group.canarywharf.com and cwg.com"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/commons-meta",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php",
     "dct:description": "generator=categorymembers (Category:One Canada Square at night, Category:Canary Wharf at night) and generator=search in the File namespace (4 searches, filetype:bitmap); prop=imageinfo, extmetadata DateTimeOriginal|LicenseShortName|Artist|ImageDescription, iiurlwidth=960; continue followed"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#source/commons-meta",
     "dcat:accessURL": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/ (thumburl)",
     "dct:description": "960 px thumbnails, kept locally only"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/lighting/press-pages.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/registry/sources/lighting/commons-photos.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/registry/lighting/%20(sitemaps,%20archived%20pages,%20colour%20sentences,%20Commons%20API%20answers,%20thumbnails,%20request%20log)"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/fetch-crown-lighting.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 node magpie/cwplans/tools/fetch-crown-lighting.mjs [--press] [--commons] [--thumbs] [--no-fetch]",
   "cwp:kind": "fetch",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Slug rule: lit, illuminated, halo, pyramid, turns-<colour>, lights-up-<colour>, light-it-, goes-<colour> (the regex is written into press-pages.json); plus a hand list of 5 pages found by search.",
    "Pages are read only as Internet Archive id_ copies (cwg.com and canarywharf.com answer scripts with an Imperva challenge; their sitemaps are served and robots.txt allows them). Kept in the committed file: URL, slug date (ddmmyy code at the end of the slug), archive URL, title, published time, the colour words that occur in sentences naming One Canada Square, a pyramid, halo, crown or tower. Page text stays in the local cache.",
    "Commons: a search hit is kept only if its title or description names the place (Canary Wharf, Canada Square, Docklands, Isle of Dogs, West India, Millwall, Blackwall, Cabot Square, Poplar); category members are kept. Use = fact only for CC BY-SA or GFDL; no image is committed.",
    "Politeness: one request at a time; at least 3 s per host for cwg.com and web.archive.org, 2 s for archive.org and the Commons API, 3 s for upload.wikimedia.org; up to 4 tries with backoff (Retry-After, else 10, 30, 90 s, at most 600 s) on 429, 5xx and resets; 2 tries for an archive copy; thumbnails stop at the first refusal (2026-10-04: 429 after 31). Failures are written to data/raw/registry/lighting/log-<date>.txt and to the page status.",
    "User-Agent glitchcan-cwplans/0.1 (https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam)."
   ],
   "cwp:network": true,
   "cwp:deterministic": false,
   "cwp:after": [],
   "cwp:area": "lighting",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "Which pages to add to the hand list (KNOWN in the tool) after a web search; recorded in press-pages.json meta.known_pages."
  },
