  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/build-trees",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "build-trees",
   "dct:description": "Joins the tree inventories, OSM trees and the Trees Outside Woodland lone-tree crowns into one list of trees in model metres, with OS Open Greenspace sites, OSM green areas and TOW canopy groups as green rings.",
   "prov:used": [
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/trees/gla-public-realm-trees-2025Nov.csv"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/trees/opgrsp_essh_tq.zip"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/trees/planning-data-tree.json"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/trees/tow-london-box.json.gz"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/docklands/greater_london-latest.osm.pbf"
    },
    {
     "@id": "urn:cwplans:local:data/raw/uk_os_OSTN15_NTv2_OSGBtoETRS.tif"
    }
   ],
   "prov:generated": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/docklands/data/trees.json"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:tool": {
    "@id": "https://github.com/danbri/glitchcan-minigam/blob/master/magpie/cwplans/tools/build-trees.mjs"
   },
   "cwp:command": "node --max-old-space-size=6000 magpie/cwplans/tools/build-trees.mjs",
   "cwp:kind": "derive",
   "cwp:rule": [
    "Box: BNG E 532400-539900, N 176700-182300 (fetch-docklands.mjs BOX_BNG); WGS84 to BNG through OSTN15; x = E - 537550, z = -(N - 180300); every value rounded to 0.5 m.",
    "Ethics (CLAUDE.md, Data ethics): a tree keeps only position, taxon (scientific and common name), height, crown spread, source and record id. Notes, sponsorship, memorial, dedication, inscription, address, owner and maintainer fields are never read into the payload; each source lists its dropped fields in sources[].dropped.",
    "Tree precedence: GLA public realm inventory first; then TPO points (planning.data), OSM natural=tree nodes and TOW Lone Tree crowns, each added only if no tree already kept lies within 3 m (TOW: within the crown radius, at least 3 m).",
    "GLA class values (\"05 to 10 m\") become the middle of the class; \"Not recorded\" is null. Species \"Unknown Tree Species\" and common name \"Plant\" give no species.",
    "TPO: records with an end date are left out; the taxon is read only from Tower Hamlets names of the form \"Common (Scientific)\"; Southwark names (site descriptions, URLs) are dropped.",
    "OSM: species, else taxon, else genus (with the :en names); height under 60 m and diameter_crown under 40 m kept.",
    "TOW Lone Tree: centroid of the polygon, height = maxht, crown = diameter of a circle with the polygon area (tow_area_m). Group of Trees, Small Woodland and NFI OHC polygons become greens with meanht.",
    "Greens are clipped to the box (Sutherland-Hodgman) and simplified (Douglas-Peucker 0.5 m; TOW 1.5 m, its outlines follow the 1 m LiDAR grid); OSM multipolygon inner rings and shapefile holes are kept as holes.",
    "Network for the source files: see fetch-trees."
   ],
   "cwp:network": false,
   "cwp:deterministic": true,
   "cwp:after": [
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/fetch-trees"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/fetch-docklands-osm"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/fetch-raw-grid"
    }
   ],
   "cwp:area": "trees",
   "cwp:fault": [],
   "cwp:judgement": "The 35 m cut-off for \"lone trees\" that are cranes or structures is applied on the page, not in the file; the source precedence order is a judgement."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/magpie/cwplans/data-register.json#activity/drone-flight",
   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "drone-flight",
   "dct:description": "Plans a synthetic drone flight over the Canary Wharf estate in the 3D model for splat training captures, checks it against limits, and optionally writes the path, a plan and a coverage estimate.",
   "prov:used": [
