   "@type": "prov:Activity",
   "rdfs:label": "Crown lighting policy, campaigns and dated colour observations",
   "dct:description": "Web searches for how the colour of One Canada Square's top is chosen, its lighting systems, campaigns and contractors; each fact written in our own words with its URL, date and how it was read. Commons thumbnails and the owner's photos of 3 October 2026 looked at by eye: what is lit (pyramid faces, halo band, facade wash, nothing) and its colour; an approximate hex from the mean of the brightest 20% of pixels in the lit area (30% for dim pyramids).",
   "prov:used": [
